.TH CHARTS 1 "2026" "charts 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
charts \- DOS-style charts and slide decks for the Linux console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B charts
.I DECK.json
.br
.B charts
.RI [ options ] " FILE" ...
.br
.B charts
.I DECK.json
.BR \-\-check " | " \-\-png
.IR FILE " | "
.B \-\-png\-dir
.IR DIR " | " \fB\-\-print\fR " | " \fB\-\-launcher\fR " " \fINAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B charts
draws bar, line, area, pie, scatter and histogram charts in sixteen colours
with dithered shading, and presents decks of them: slides of charts, text,
big numbers, flow diagrams and free shapes, paged through with the arrow
keys.
.PP
A deck is a JSON file with a "slides" array, usually written by an agent or a
script.  Data files are CSV, TSV or JSON.  Given a deck on a terminal,
.B charts
opens the presenter.  Given data files it prints one chart each, or with
.B \-i
opens them in the presenter, a slide each.
.PP
The presenter draws real pixels on the Linux console through the framebuffer
.RI ( /dev/fb0 ,
which needs membership of the
.I video
group), uses the kitty graphics protocol or sixel inside terminals that have
them, and falls back to half-block characters anywhere else.  The picture is
the same in each.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS What to do
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-show
open data files in the presenter
.TP
.B \-\-print
print to standard output as text (the default for data files)
.TP
.BI \-\-png " FILE"
write one slide as a PNG; see
.B \-\-slide
.TP
.BI \-\-png\-dir " DIR"
write every slide as DIR/slide\-NN.png
.TP
.BR \-\-check " [" \-\-json ]
validate a deck; every problem is reported with its JSON path
.TP
.B \-\-describe
print what was parsed: a deck's outline, or a data file's columns
.TP
.BI \-\-launcher " NAME"
write a small sh script that presents the deck, to ~/.local/bin/NAME (or to
NAME itself when it has a slash), and print its path; it opens a terminal
when started without one
.TP
.BI \-\-slide " N"
the slide (from 1) to print, render or open on
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE"
write \-\-print output to FILE
.TP
.BR \-\-schema ", " \-\-example " [csv|json|deck], " \-\-list\-types ", " \-\-list\-palettes ", " \-\-list\-themes
reference output
.TP
.B \-\-demo
present a deck built into the binary, all its data inline: the quickest look
.SS How it looks
.TP
.BI \-t " NAME" "\fR[,\fINAME\fR]"
chart type: bar stacked hbar dumbbell line area pie pie3d donut scatter hist table
.TP
.BI \-T " TEXT" "\fR, \fB\-\-subtitle\fR, \fB\-\-xlabel\fR, \fB\-\-ylabel\fR"
titles and axis labels
.TP
.BI \-p " NAME"
series palette: dos ega cga ice fire green amber mono
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " NAME"
dos, black or light
.TP
.BR \-\-values ", " \-\-legend ", " \-\-grid ", " \-\-shadow
and
.B \-\-no\-...
to turn each off
.TP
.BI \-\-frame " STYLE"
double, single, heavy or none
.TP
.BI \-\-depth " N"
3-D extrusion, 0 to 6; 0 is flat
.TP
.BR \-\-explode " [" \fIN\fR ]
pop pie slice N out; bare, the biggest
.TP
.BI \-\-min " V" "\fR, \fB\-\-max \fIV\fR, \fB\-\-prec \fIN\fR, \fB\-\-bins \fIN\fR"
axis limits, decimals, histogram buckets
.TP
.BI \-w " N" "\fR, \fB\-H \fIN\fR, \fB\-\-size \fICOLSxROWS\fR"
size in character cells; \-\-png and \-\-check default to 120x33
(80x29, the VGA slide area, on DOS)
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " K"
pixel multiplier for \-\-png and the pixel displays
.TP
.BI \-\-gfx " MODE"
auto, fb, kitty, sixel, cells, ascii or vga (DOS)
.TP
.BR \-\-ascii ", " \-\-color ", " \-\-no\-color ", " \-\-tile
plain ASCII; colour; all files on one slide
.SS How the data is read
.BR \-\-xy ", " \-\-transpose ", " \-\-no\-header ", "
.BI \-\-delim " C" \fR,
.BI \-\-labels\-col " N" \fR,
.BI \-\-series\-col " N" \fR,
.BI \-\-label\-key " K"
.SH KEYS
.TS
l l.
left right space pgup pgdn	previous / next slide
home end, digits enter	first / last / go to a slide
o  n  ?	overview, speaker notes, key list
tab	focus the next block
e	edit the focused chart's data, or a text block
a	annotate the chart
t p v l g d x	type, palette, values, legend, grid, depth, explode
i c N E X	add text, add chart, new slide, edit title, delete block
y  s  r  q	theme, save, reload, quit
.TE
.PP
In the sheet: arrows move, typing replaces a cell, enter edits, ins adds a row,
^D deletes one, ^A adds a series, ^X deletes one, u undoes, s saves, esc
returns.  In annotate mode: left/right pick the point, up/down the series,
enter writes a note, h a line across, v a mark, del removes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 the input has errors; 2 the command line is wrong.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CHARTS_GFX
as \-\-gfx
.TP
.BR CHARTS_FB ", " FRAMEBUFFER
framebuffer device, default /dev/fb0
.TP
.B CHARTS_FB_GEOM
WxHxBPP: treat CHARTS_FB as a plain file of that shape
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
turn colour off
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/DECK.md, docs/INPUT.md, docs/AGENT.md in the source tree;
.B charts \-\-schema
